comments.body:
@sepo-agent /answer 

another small issue: on the main content page (https://augmented-mind-augmented-mind-pr-66-18f9f9.surge.sh/livestreams/ls01), the livestreams section is outside of the page region and there is no scrolling for that. 

What do you think could be a proper fix for it?

I found the root cause. Here's my analysis and a proposed fix.

## Root cause

On content pages, the left sidebar is laid out as a **fixed-height sticky flex column** with no overflow handling — see [`quartz/styles/base.scss` L221–229](https://github.com/augmented-mind/augmented-mind.github.io/blob/pr-66/quartz/styles/base.scss#L221-L229):

```scss
& .sidebar {
  gap: 1.2rem;
  top: 0;
  height: 100vh;        // pinned to viewport height
  position: sticky;
  display: flex;
  // ← no overflow-y, so anything past 100vh just spills out invisibly
}
```

This PR now stacks **two** `RecentNotes` lists in that sidebar — `episodesSection` and `livestreamsSection`, each with `limit: 20` ([`quartz.layout.ts` L71–72](https://github.com/augmented-mind/augmented-mind.github.io/blob/pr-66/quartz.layout.ts#L71-L72)). On the `ls01` page the combined height of `PageTitle` + search row + Episodes list + Livestreams list exceeds `100vh`, and since the sidebar is `height: 100vh` with no `overflow-y`, the Livestreams list at the bottom gets clipped off-screen with no way to scroll to it. (On mobile it's fine — those lists render in `afterBody` and flow with the page.)

## Proposed fix

**Option A — make the sidebar scrollable (smallest, most robust).** One rule in `base.scss`:

```scss
& .sidebar.left {
  overflow-y: auto;
}
```

The sidebar stays pinned at `100vh`, but its contents now scroll internally when they overflow. This handles any future growth (more episodes/streams) without further tuning. I'd pair it with a thin/subtle scrollbar style so it doesn't look heavy.

**Option B — keep title/search pinned, scroll only the lists.** Wrap the two `RecentNotes` lists in a flex-growing container with `min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto`, leaving `PageTitle` and the search row fixed at top. Nicer UX, but needs a small layout/container change rather than pure CSS.

**Option C (complementary, not a real fix) — lower the sidebar `limit`** (e.g. `20 → 5`) so two lists fit. Reduces the chance of overflow but doesn't actually solve it; I'd only do this alongside A.

## My recommendation

Go with **Option A** now — it's a one-line, low-risk CSS change that directly fixes the reported clipping, scoped to `.sidebar.left` so the right sidebar is untouched. We can layer Option B later if we want the title/search to stay pinned.

### Execution plan
1. Add `overflow-y: auto` to `.sidebar.left` in [`quartz/styles/base.scss`](https://github.com/augmented-mind/augmented-mind.github.io/blob/pr-66/quartz/styles/base.scss#L231) (desktop branch only — the mobile media query already sets `position: initial; height: unset`, so it's unaffected).
2. Add a light custom scrollbar style so the internal scroll looks intentional.
3. Rebuild and verify on `/livestreams/ls01` that both Episodes and Livestreams lists are reachable, and confirm no regression on episode pages or the index.

Want me to implement Option A? Or would you prefer Option B (pinned header, scrollable lists) for the nicer UX?

---
